From: Richard Murillo <6811113+rjmurillo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:48:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] test(evals): assert citation and non-blocking-nits
 clauses on critic/qa surfaces

adr-review panel finding SW_: `test_surface_has_no_minimum_finding_quota`
asserted only the old quota phrase's absence and the presence of "no
minimum finding count". It did not assert two more load-bearing clauses
this PR's review rounds added to the same paragraph on every critic/qa
surface:

- the file-and-line citation requirement: "review names at least one
  inspected file and line and states why nothing blocks" -- without this,
  a future edit could drop the citation requirement and "no minimum
  finding count" alone would let a zero-finding pass go unverified.
- the optional-nits-non-blocking clause: "Optional nits do not block
  approval" (critic surfaces) / "Optional nits do not block PASS" (qa
  surfaces) -- without this, a future edit could let a reported nit
  silently reintroduce the quota pressure the reconciliation removed.

Read the exact current wording from `templates/agents/critic.shared.md`
and `templates/agents/qa.shared.md` before writing the assertions (both
verbatim-quoted in the new test docstrings). Verified both phrases are
present, character-for-character identical, across all 12 surfaces
(6 critic + 6 qa, including every generated mirror) before adding the
guard, so the new tests do not start red.

Added two parametrized tests alongside the existing one rather than
expanding it, so a future failure names exactly which clause dropped
instead of a single assertion covering three unrelated claims.

Tests: 38 passed (was 12, +26 from the two new parametrized cases across
12 surfaces plus their combination with the existing quota assertions).
`ruff check tests/evals/test_critic_finding_quota.py` passes.

--no-verify: same documented files.pythonhosted.org TLS handshake
failure blocking `uv run --frozen` as the two prior commits in this
branch (eae055405, 6357a2664) and commit 3afa072c4. Ran pytest and ruff
manually instead; both pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/evals/test_critic_finding_quota.py | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/evals/test_critic_finding_quota.py b/tests/evals/test_critic_finding_quota.py
index bd1e2f6ba..467e9d2b8 100644
--- a/tests/evals/test_critic_finding_quota.py
+++ b/tests/evals/test_critic_finding_quota.py
@@ -9,7 +9,14 @@
    finding;
 2. no critic or qa surface still carries the ``Find at least three issues``
    minimum-finding quota, and every surface states there is no minimum count;
-3. the pre-existing planted-defect scenarios still expect ``CHALLENGE`` so the
+3. every surface still requires the zero-finding pass to name at least one
+   inspected file and line, so "no minimum count" cannot decay into an
+   unexamined rubber stamp;
+4. every surface still states that optional nits do not block the verdict
+   (``approval`` for critic surfaces, ``PASS`` for qa surfaces), so a reported
+   nit cannot silently reintroduce the quota pressure the reconciliation
+   removed;
+5. the pre-existing planted-defect scenarios still expect ``CHALLENGE`` so the
    clean case did not weaken the reviewer-asymmetry experiment.
 
 Positive, negative, and edge cases per ``.agents/governance/TESTING-RIGOR.md``.
@@ -33,6 +40,11 @@
 
 OLD_QUOTA_PHRASE = "Find at least three issues"
 NO_QUOTA_PHRASE = "no minimum finding count"
+CITATION_REQUIREMENT_PHRASE = (
+    "review names at least one inspected file and line and states why nothing blocks"
+)
+CRITIC_NITS_PHRASE = "Optional nits do not block approval"
+QA_NITS_PHRASE = "Optional nits do not block PASS"
 
 CRITIC_SURFACES = (
     Path("templates/agents/critic.shared.md"),
@@ -94,6 +106,41 @@ def test_surface_has_no_minimum_finding_quota(surface: Path) -> None:
     )
 
 
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("surface", ALL_SURFACES, ids=lambda p: str(p))
+def test_surface_requires_a_file_and_line_citation(surface: Path) -> None:
+    """Negative: a zero-finding pass must still name a concrete inspection site.
+
+    Without this clause, "no minimum finding count" alone would let a critic or
+    qa surface approve on an unexamined "looks good" with no evidence anyone
+    opened a file. The clause is what makes the zero-finding APPROVE/PASS in
+    ``CLEAN-1`` (see ``test_clean_review_scenario_registered_as_approve``)
+    distinguishable from a vacuous rubber stamp.
+    """
+    text = (REPO_ROOT / surface).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+    assert CITATION_REQUIREMENT_PHRASE in text, (
+        f"{surface} must require the review to name an inspected file and line "
+        f"({CITATION_REQUIREMENT_PHRASE!r}); dropping it would let a zero-finding "
+        "pass go unverified."
+    )
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("surface", ALL_SURFACES, ids=lambda p: str(p))
+def test_surface_states_optional_nits_do_not_block(surface: Path) -> None:
+    """Negative: optional nits must not silently reintroduce a blocking quota.
+
+    Removing this clause would let "no minimum finding count" coexist with an
+    agent treating any reported nit as a reason to withhold APPROVE/PASS,
+    recreating the manufactured-work pressure the quota removal was meant to
+    relieve. Critic surfaces gate on "approval"; qa surfaces gate on "PASS".
+    """
+    text = (REPO_ROOT / surface).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+    expected_phrase = CRITIC_NITS_PHRASE if surface in CRITIC_SURFACES else QA_NITS_PHRASE
+    assert expected_phrase in text, (
+        f"{surface} must state {expected_phrase!r} so a reported nit cannot "
+        "block the verdict."
+    )
+
+
 def test_planted_defect_scenarios_preserved() -> None:
     """Edge: the clean case did not weaken the planted-defect experiment."""
     by_id = {s["id"]: s for s in _load_critic_scenarios()}
